---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import PostHog from '../components/posthog.astro';
import '../styles/design-system.css';
const pilot = 'mailto:ben@keystonemere.com?subject=Aether%20Environmental%20Canvas%20Pilot';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Explore adaptive environmental displays, real-time rendering and commercial pilots with Aether Environmental Canvas."/><title>Environmental Canvas | Aether</title><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg"/><PostHog /></head>
<body><SiteHeader/><main id="main">
<section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Aether Environmental Canvas</p><h1>A living environment for your space.</h1><p class="lead">Turn a commercial display into an evolving landscape, with configurable weather, gentle motion and scheduled changes in atmosphere.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#demonstrations">Explore live scenes</a><a class="button" href={pilot}>Request a pilot</a></div></div><figure><img src="/scene-lab/ullswater/ullswater-background.jpg" alt="Lake and mountains in the Ullswater Retreat demonstration" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Ullswater Retreat · Aether demonstration environment</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="demonstrations" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Experience the technology</p><h2>Two environments. One rendering approach.</h2><p>Explore working demonstrations directly in your browser. Each opens separately so the product page stays lightweight.</p><div class="grid two"><article><img class="preview" src="/scene-lab/ullswater/ullswater-background.jpg" alt="Ullswater lake landscape" loading="lazy"/><div class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">Lake District inspired</p><h3>Ullswater Retreat</h3><p>Rainfall, water ripples and lake vapour bring a landscape to life.</p><a class="button primary" href="/scene-lab/ullswater/?player=1&amp;quality=pi4&amp;weather=auto" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Launch Ullswater (new tab)</a></div></article><article class="garden"><div class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">Scheduled atmosphere</p><h3>Living Garden</h3><p>Explore a garden environment with changing atmospheric cues driven by the existing signage scheduler.</p><a class="button" href="/display/demo/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Launch Living Garden (new tab)</a></div></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Beyond the video loop</p><h2>Change the atmosphere, not the video file.</h2><div class="grid two"><article class="inner"><h3>Fixed video playback</h3><p>A prerecorded sequence repeats. Changing its visual content typically requires another video or an edited asset.</p></article><article class="inner accent"><h3>Aether environmental rendering</h3><p>Scene imagery and visual effects are combined in the browser. Supported parameters can change independently of the underlying image.</p></article></div><div class="grid three states"><article class="inner"><h3>Weather</h3><p>Adjust supported rainfall, vapour and other scene effects.</p></article><article class="inner"><h3>Motion</h3><p>Configure effect intensity to suit the environment.</p></article><article class="inner"><h3>Time</h3><p>Use scheduled scene states to vary atmosphere throughout the day.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section location"><img src="/images/commercial/hotel-lobby.webp" alt="AI-generated concept of a hotel lobby with an environmental display" loading="lazy"/><div><p class="eyebrow">Collection direction</p><h2>Rooted in the location.</h2><p>Our planned collections will reflect the geography and visual identity of each venue. A hotel could commission a landscape inspired by its surroundings, subject to asset rights and production scope.</p><p class="micro">AI-generated installation concept, not a completed customer installation.</p><a href="/solutions/">Explore commercial applications →</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Deployment architecture</p><h2>Designed for lightweight display hardware.</h2><div class="grid three"><article class="inner"><h3>Browser-native</h3><p>Local visual rendering without a continuous video stream.</p></article><article class="inner"><h3>Device profiles</h3><p>Rendering settings can be tuned to supported hardware and display requirements.</p></article><article class="inner"><h3>Operational resilience</h3><p>Render monitoring and recovery mechanisms are undergoing pilot validation.</p></article></div><p><a href="/technology/">Explore the technology →</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">Commercial pilot programme</p><h2>From display assessment to pilot review.</h2><div class="grid two"><article class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Assess</p><h3>Understand the venue</h3><p>Agree display location, hardware, viewing conditions and visual direction.</p></article><article class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Configure</p><h3>Prepare the environment</h3><p>Choose a demonstration scene and appropriate rendering settings.</p></article><article class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Evaluate</p><h3>Run an agreed pilot</h3><p>Assess visual quality, playback stability and recovery against agreed criteria.</p></article><article class="inner"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Review</p><h3>Define ongoing deployment</h3><p>Agree support, content rights, hardware and commercial terms before expansion.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="closing"><h2>Explore Aether for your venue.</h2><p>Commercial deployment is under validation. Pilot availability and specifications are agreed individually.</p><a class="button primary" href={pilot}>Request a pilot</a></section>
</main><SiteFooter/></body></html>
<style>
:global(html){background:#070b12;color:#f4f7ff;font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif}:global(body){background:radial-gradient(circle at 85% 3%,#172742 0%,transparent 34%),#070b12;color:#f4f7ff}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:48px 20px 40px}h1,h2,h3{letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1.12}h1{font-size:clamp(42px,5.6vw,76px);margin:15px 0 24px}h2{font-size:clamp(29px,3.5vw,46px);margin:12px 0 20px}h3{font-size:23px;margin:10px 0}p{color:#b8c7dc;line-height:1.65}.lead{font-size:clamp(17px,1.8vw,21px)}.eyebrow{color:#7dd3fc;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:800}.hero,.location{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px;align-items:center}.hero figure{margin:0;border:1px solid #334961;border-radius:18px;overflow:hidden;background:#101b2c}.hero img,.preview,.location img{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover}figcaption{padding:14px;color:#b8c7dc;font-size:13px}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:26px}.button{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #48607b;border-radius:999px;padding:12px 18px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;color:#f4f7ff}.button:hover{background:#213149}.primary{background:#d9f5ed;color:#092019;border-color:#d9f5ed}.primary:hover{background:#bcebdc}.section{border-top:1px solid #243248;padding-top:40px;margin:58px 0}.grid{display:grid;gap:16px;margin-top:24px}.two{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}article,.closing{background:#101b2c;border:1px solid #2b4059;border-radius:16px;overflow:hidden}.inner{padding:26px}.garden{display:flex;align-items:center;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at top right,#23443d,#101b2c 75%)}.accent{border-color:#60988b}.location img{border-radius:16px}.micro{font-size:12px}.section a:not(.button){color:#8edfff}.closing{text-align:center;padding:40px 24px}.closing .button{margin-top:10px}a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #7dd3fc;outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:760px){.hero,.location,.two,.three{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding-top:24px}.section{margin:40px 0}.inner{padding:20px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){:global(html){scroll-behavior:auto}}
</style>
